    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look poised for a high-ceiling outing today, led by the elite matchup profile of **Gunnar Henderson** (81.00). Facing Cade Cavalli, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an ideal combination of a leadoff spot and a significant platoon advantage, making him our primary engine for Runs and RBI. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Heliot Ramos** (65.50) also present as high-leverage starts; **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on dynamic platoon splits against Chris Bassitt, while **Heliot Ramos** enjoys a combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and a soft SP_xERA from Luis Severino. **Kyle Tucker** (66.72) remains a mandatory start as well, with wind conditions blowing out providing the necessary marginal utility to elevate his floor.\n\nWhile our lineup is aggressive, we are closely monitoring the status of **Jackson Merrill** (52.77). Despite his prime leadoff role, he faces a daunting task against Logan Gilbert (2.98 xERA), which suppresses his scoring ceiling. The tightest decision on the bench involved **Josh Jung** (48.45), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Miguel Vargas** (55.06). While **Josh Jung** offers decent situational upside, the optimizer leaned toward **Miguel Vargas** due to his projected #3 spot in the lineup against Jameson Taillon, providing a higher opportunity for RBI production compared to the lower-rung utility options. \n\nWe must remain cautious regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status across our roster, as sudden changes to batting orders will drastically shift the daily efficiency scores. **Nasim Nunez** (53.88) and **Brady House** (55.38) are particularly sensitive to these shifts while facing Chris Bassitt; their value is heavily tied to their sprint speed and ability to navigate Bassitt\u2019s pitch mix, but both are at risk if their defensive-focused slots fall further down the lineup. Managers should monitor weather updates at the parks housing **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages**, as the current wind advantage could evaporate if forecasts shift before first pitch.",
